(8,'KEEP',[I,II],'numerical','Normal modes of a discretized hanging rope','Newton force balance, tension from supported weights, small-angle oscillations and matrix/continuum limits determine the modes and spectral sums. Flexible-string waves are conventional; no bending stiffness is introduced.'),
(9,'KEEP',[I],'numerical','Rope shape and edge wear with explicit bending and abrasion laws','Curvature proportional to torque and wear speed proportional to contact force are both supplied. Local force/torque balance and geometric differentiation determine elastica and moving-boundary wear; no unsupplied constitutive bending law need be known.'),
