(12,'BORDERLINE',[I],'theory','Inferring smoke-ring direction from the supplied photograph','The actual embedded torus image is present and inspected. A qualitative parcel-circulation and momentum explanation may use ordinary mechanics, but inferring propagation from smoke texture can require unsupplied vortex-flow induction and is visually ambiguous. Intended depth is unresolved.'),
(13,'BORDERLINE',[I,IV],'theory','Comparing melting times in fresh and salt water','Calorimetry, density-driven convection and melting/freezing arguments are foundational, but a quantitative time ratio also requires a declared mixing/heat-transfer and saline-property model absent from the statement. The qualitative and quantitative work is inseparable here.'),
(14,'KEEP',[I,III],'data_analysis','Pressure from resolved gas-particle collision velocities','Individual momentum jumps, spherical impact geometry and kinetic-gas momentum flux connect measured velocity changes and total time to pressure. The supplied Einstein relation is context; no stochastic master equation is needed.'),
